ng. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ce2360a-708f-4b2b-9c9d-ca5111f241aa","uuid":"4104be2c-b78b-463e-9523-b8ad68a8ec23","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json","content":"{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n  },\n  \"structure\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n      \"title\": null,\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"start_position\": 28,\n      \"end_position\": 13811,\n      \"word_count\": 2443,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n        \"Courtiers\",\n        \"Musicians\",\n        \"Buffoons\",\n        \"Improvisatori\",\n        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n        \"Beauty\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by sharp pains, profuse bleeding, and scarlet stains that isolate victims from all sympathy. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers into his fortified, abbey-like palace, sealing all entrances and providing endless entertainment to distract from the horror outside. Within the palace, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored chambers, each with stained-glass windows matching their decor, culminating in a black room with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, silencing the music and unsettling the guests. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—covered in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask—enters, and despite the prince’s furious command to seize him, no one dares intervene as the figure calmly traverses all seven rooms. The prince, enraged and terrified, pursues the figure with a dagger into the black chamber, where the figure turns and the prince collapses dead; the courtiers then discover the figure is empty, revealing the Red Death itself has infiltrated their sanctuary, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"84a30955-671f-4385-9874-e8ec29084c89\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the mummer\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 4,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 18,\n      \"first_po