{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01XqvhzueHgpg1haDdtKBBZD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Evaluation Complete\n\n**Result: FAIL (6.70/10)** - Below threshold of 8.0\n\n### Summary\n\nAttempt 16 for \"The Masque of the Red Death\" failed. The post-processing death evidence split function that was added did not trigger, and the character extraction score remains critically low at 3/10.\n\n### Key Findings\n\n| Category | Score | Notes |\n|----------|-------|-------|\n| Structure Detection | 10/10 | Correct - single continuous story |\n| Character Extraction | 3/10 | **CRITICAL** - \"Prospero\" merged with \"the mummer\" (antagonist) instead of \"Prince Prospero\" (protagonist) |\n| Character Profiles | 5/10 | Empty profiles for all characters |\n| Chapter Summaries | 9/10 | Excellent - correctly identifies both characters as separate! |\n| Pronunciation Guide | 6/10 | ~35-40% false positives |\n| HTML Presentation | 8/10 | Functional and well-organized |\n\n### Root Cause Identified\n\nThe fundamental problem is that the LLM pairwise merge decision is making the wrong choice:\n- **\"Prospero\"** (4 mentions) should be an alias of **\"Prince Prospero\"** (3 mentions) ← same person\n- But the LLM is merging **\"Prospero\"** with **\"the mummer\"** (3 mentions) ← WRONG: protagonist vs antagonist\n\n### Recommended Fix for Attempt 17\n\n**Pre-merge substring matching heuristic:**\n- Before sending pairs to the LLM, check if name A is a substring of name B\n- If \"Prospero\" is a substring of \"Prince Prospero\", pre-merge them before LLM decisions\n- This prevents the LLM from making the wrong merge with \"the mummer\"\n\nLocation: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py`\n\n### Next Action\n\nRun `PROMPT_fix.md` to implement pre-merge substring matching to fix the \"Prospero\" → \"Prince Prospero\" grouping before LLM pairwise decisions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null